        "standfirst": "Brentford beat Chelsea 3-0, three second-half goals lifting Keith Andrews's unbeaten side above the visitors and into third.",
        "account": "Igor Thiago had the first sight of goal after five minutes, meeting a Yehor Yarmoliuk cross with a shot that flew off target.\nPedro Neto replied for Chelsea after 10 minutes, working a chance from a Danny Welbeck pass, but Caoimhín Kelleher saved.\nJust before half-time Keane Lewis-Potter was set up by Jaidon Anthony, only for his shot to be turned away.\nThe opening goal came after 61 minutes. Jannik Schuster headed a corner across goal and Jaidon Anthony finished for 1-0.\nWith seven minutes left Thiago made it 2-0 on the break, Brentford's second in the space of 11 minutes.\nFábio Carvalho came on three minutes from time.\nFour minutes into added time Carvalho added the third. From within the six-yard box he swept a right-footed finish into the top corner for 3-0.",
